# Assumptions: this covers adult inpatient intravenous medication administration in a barcode-enabled hospital.
# Barriers are procedural and technical controls before and after an incorrect dose reaches the patient.
bowtie "Patient medication error"
hazard "High-alert intravenous medication"
topevent "Incorrect medication or dose administered"
threat "Look-alike or sound-alike drug selection"
  prevent "Tall-man lettering and segregated storage"
  prevent "Pharmacy verification"
threat "Incorrect prescription entry"
  prevent "Computerised dose-range checking"
    escalation "Alert fatigue overrides warning"
      barrier "High-severity alert governance"
  prevent "Independent prescriber review"
threat "Patient identification error"
  prevent "Two-identifier bedside check"
  prevent "Barcode medication administration"
consequence "Acute adverse drug reaction"
  mitigate "Continuous patient monitoring"
  mitigate "Rapid-response team"
consequence "Delayed treatment or recovery"
  mitigate "Medication reconciliation and review"
  mitigate "Clinical pharmacist consultation"
consequence "Permanent patient harm"
  mitigate "Antidote and emergency protocol"
